# Brand consistency — everything customers see or receive

Any surface a customer **sees or receives** must feel like the same NoorLink brand: website, Insider newsletter (web + email), transactional emails, support replies chrome, promo cards, and CTAs.

## Tokens (single source of truth)

| Role | Value | Use |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Primary teal | `#0F3D3E` | Headers, brand chrome, strong UI |
| Ink / dark | `#05191A` | Text on orange CTAs, deep footer only |
| Accent orange | `#FF9500` | CTAs, kickers, wordmark accent |
| Page / email bg | `#F3F5F7` | Outer canvas |
| Surface | `#FFFFFF` / light mist `#F3F7F7` | Cards with readable body copy |
| Body text | `#111827` / `#334155` | Paragraphs on light surfaces |
| Muted | `#6B7280` / `#5B6B6C` | Secondary lines |

Frontend: `styles/tokens.css` + Insider vars in `styles/insider.css`.  
Emails: `app/services/email_brand.py` in noorlink-automation — **do not invent new colors**.

## Readability rule (non-negotiable)

- **Never** put dark slate / teal body text on near-black cards.
- Deal / promo / link cards that contain readable copy + CTAs use a **light surface** (white / mist), teal code text, orange primary CTA (`#FF9500` on `#05191A` text), outlined secondary links in teal.
- Dark teal is for **headers / hero chrome / footers**, not for dense paragraph + multi-link blocks.

## Tone & content

- Calm, practical, trustworthy — travel advisor energy, not hype.
- Same voice in monthly Insider, specials, order emails, reminders, and on-site copy.
- Prefer “install before you fly” over fake urgency.
- Wordmark: **Noor** (teal) + **Link** (orange).

## When changing one surface

If you restyle a deal card, CTA, or promo block on the **site**, mirror it in the **email** templates (and vice versa) in the same change set whenever possible.
